  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: 
    basic: GLP1-R is a receptor. A receptor protein sits in the cell's membrane or
      inside of the cell.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: When bound by other molecules, it changes shape (Conformational Change)
      and transmits (Signal Transduction) information to the cell.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: (Conformational Change) A change in a macromolecule's shape, frequently
      caused by something in its environment. This change often affects the molecule's
      function.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: (Signal Transduction) The process by which a cell receives information
      from outside and transmits that information through a series of molecules inside.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: GLP1 is the endogenous ligand for GLP1R, while other molecules can activate
      GLP1-R too, resulting in similar or different effects.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
